course: dictionary
lesson: 15349
title: Solidarity: standing together
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Solidarity means standing together and supporting each other. People show solidarity when they share the same goals, problems or feelings. «The whole class wore blue ribbons in solidarity with Mia, who had moved to a new school.» The class was not just being kind once: they showed they were on Mia's side.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. Who is supporting whom, and what is the problem? «The villagers showed solidarity with the families whose homes had flooded, bringing food and blankets.» The helpers were not in the flood, but they supported the people who were. That is solidarity too.
explain: Solidarity is uncountable, so you do not say «a solidarity». You can show solidarity, or act in solidarity with someone. To check your meaning, swap in the words «standing together and supporting». If the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: Solidarity means standing together and supporting each other.
fact: Useful phrases are «in solidarity with», «show solidarity» and «a sign of solidarity».
fact: Solidarity is uncountable, so you do not say «a solidarity» or «solidarities».
fact: «Solidarity» with a capital S was a Polish trade union and freedom movement, led by Lech Wałęsa from 1980.
fact: A trade union is a group of workers who join together to protect their rights.
exercise: «The workers stood in solidarity during the strike.» What does solidarity mean here? | Winning a prize for the best team | *Standing together and supporting each other | Running away from the problem | Sleeping late in the morning
exercise: «Our school raised money in solidarity with children who had lost their homes in the storm.» What does solidarity show? | Sadness about the weather | Anger at the storm | *Support for people in trouble, from people who are not in that trouble
exercise: «Ella wore a red scarf as a sign of solidarity with her friend.» Find the word that tells you Ella was supporting her friend. | *solidarity | wore | scarf | red
test: «The rowers stood in solidarity with their coach, who had been unfairly blamed.» What does solidarity show about the rowers? | They went home early | *They supported the coach by standing with him | They forgot the rules | They were angry with the coach
test: Which sentence uses solidarity correctly? | Let's buy three solidarities at the shop | *The neighbours showed solidarity by helping the family whose shop had burned down | The solidarity ate three sandwiches for lunch | We went to solidarity on Tuesday
exam: What was Solidarity, with a capital S? | A football club in Warsaw | *A Polish trade union and freedom movement led by Lech Wałęsa from 1980 | A famous painting in a Polish museum | A type of Polish bread
